{"shortDescription":"By Avinash  PLatin American currencies were mixed on Wednesday against a steady U.S. dollar ahead of a Federal Reserve policy decision, while lower oil prices weighed on Brazilian stocks before a local central bank meeting.MSCI's index tracking LatAm FX (.MILA00000CUS) edged up 0.2%, while a corres…","astDescription":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"p","children":["By Avinash  P"]},{"type":"p","children":["Latin American currencies were mixed on Wednesday against a steady U.S. dollar ahead of a Federal Reserve policy decision, while lower oil prices weighed on Brazilian stocks before a local central bank meeting."]},{"type":"p","children":["MSCI's index tracking LatAm FX (.MILA00000CUS) edged up 0.2%, while a corresponding stocks gauge (.MILA00000PUS) dipped 0.3%."]},{"type":"p","children":["Oil prices slipped as reports that Saudi Arabia was offering additional crude cargoes via Oman eased concerns about the scale of Middle East supply disruptions."]},{"type":"p","children":["Elevated crude prices have supported risk sentiment towards net oil exporters such as Brazil and Colombia."]},{"type":"p","children":["Brazil's stock index ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV","text":"BMFBOVESPA:IBOV"}}," was down 0.3%, with state oil producer Petrobras falling 3.5%. The real ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDBRL","text":"FX_IDC:USDBRL"}}," added 0.2% ahead of Wednesday's interest rate decision."]},{"type":"p","children":["The Monetary Policy Committee, Copom, is expected to cut Brazil's Selic benchmark rate by 25 basis points for a fifth straight meeting, to 13.75%, according to a Reuters poll."]},{"type":"p","children":["\"August's IPCA (inflation data) continues to indicate a benign inflation environment, supported by declines in electricity tariffs, gasoline prices, airfares, and food prices. As a result, August's reading kept the door open for a 25 bp cut in the Selic rate,\" Rabobank analysts said in a note."]},{"type":"p","children":["Investors are also mindful of political developments in Brazil, with opinion polls indicating a tight presidential election battle between incumbent Luiz Inácio Lula da Silva and challenger Flávio Bolsonaro."]},{"type":"p","children":["Separately, economic activity in Brazil fell by a seasonally adjusted 0.2% in July from the previous month, a central bank index showed."]},{"type":"p","children":["Colombia's shares ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BVC:ICAP","text":"BVC:ICAP"}}," fell 1.1%, with state-run oil firm Ecopetrol ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BVC:ECOPETROL","text":"BVC:ECOPETROL"}}," falling 2.8%. The peso ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"FX_IDC:USDCOP","text":"FX_IDC:USDCOP"}}," eased 0.7%."]},{"type":"p","children":["In Argentina, gross domestic product likely grew 1.6% year-on-year in the second quarter, according to the median estimate in a Reuters survey, slowing from 6.5% in the same period of 2025."]},{"type":"p","children":["Local stocks ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BCBA:IMV","text":"BCBA:IMV"}}," dropped 1% and the currency (ARS=RASL=) was flat."]},{"type":"p","children":["Stock markets in the region's second-largest economy, Mexico, were closed for a holiday."]},{"type":"p","children":["Elsewhere in emerging markets, Turkish stocks ",{"type":"symbol","params":{"symbol":"BIST:XU100","text":"BIST:XU100"}}," declined 5.5% to their lowest in nearly four months after the regulator's latest fund rules created liquidity pressures."]},{"type":"p","children":["In the United States, policymakers are expected to raise rates by 25 basis points, with markets also keenly waiting for comments from Chair Kevin Warsh for clues on the future policy path."]},{"type":"p","children":["Key Latin American stock indexes and currencies at 1524 GMT:"]},{"type":"table","children":[{"type":"table-body","children":[{"type":"table-row","children":[{"type":"table-data-cell","children":[{"type":"p","children":["Latin America